course: dictionary
lesson: 1520
title: Centimetres and the metre
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A centimetre is a small unit of length, about the width of a fingernail. It is used to measure short things like pencils, shells and the sides of shapes. «The Greenland shark grows about a centimetre a year.» That tells you a centimetre is a very small step on a measuring scale.
explain: Units of length fit together. 10 millimetres make 1 centimetre, and 100 centimetres make 1 metre. So a metre is 100 centimetres long. When you see «60 centimetres», you can picture it as a bit more than half a metre.
explain: The short word is cm, and you write it after the number, like 8 cm. Centimetre is the British spelling. Some countries, such as the USA, write centimeter. Both mean the same thing. When you measure an area, you use «square centimetres» (cm²), which measures a flat space, not just a line.
fact: A centimetre is a unit of length, written cm.
fact: 10 millimetres make 1 centimetre.
fact: 100 centimetres make 1 metre.
fact: «Centimetre» is the British spelling; some countries write «centimeter».
fact: Area is measured in «square centimetres» (cm²), and volume in «cubic centimetres» (cm³).
exercise: «The Greenland shark grows about a centimetre a year.» How much does it grow each year? | *About a centimetre | About a kilometre | About ten metres | About a metre
exercise: How many centimetres make 1 metre? | 1000 | 50 | *100 | 10
exercise: The area is measured in «square centimetres» (cm²). Which unit is used for area? | *Square centimetres | Kilograms | Litres | Centimetres
test: «The giant anteater's tongue is about 60 centimetres long.» Is that more or less than half a metre? | Exactly 1 metre | Less than 1 centimetre | Less than half a metre | *More than half a metre
test: How many millimetres are in 1 centimetre? | 100 | 1 | *10 | 1000
exam: «Megalodon's teeth grew up to 17 centimetres long.» How many millimetres is 17 centimetres? | *170 mm | 70 mm | 17 mm | 1700 mm
